  "plain": "Scott Ramsay, who researches a flying saucer said to have crashed near Aztec, New Mexico in 1948, refers back to the original story about it by a writer, Frank Scully. He says there were two sets of photographs of the crash, and that the set the government took did not last long, fading to blank. If true, it would explain why official pictures of the crash never surfaced."
